      "image": null,
      "content": "Generative LLMs dominate the headlines, but running full autoregressive token decoding just to determine a classification or routing step is an expensive architectural anti-pattern. That mismatch explains the surge of interest in dedicated decision models.\n\nUnlike traditional text generation APIs where output tokens drive the bulk of your latency and spend, decision architectures function as open-domain zero-shot classifiers. By framing prompts as structured states evaluated against explicit labels, the inference pass evaluates logits directly across candidate classes rather than autoregressively predicting variable-length tokens.\n\nThis breakdown analyzes Perplexity Decider v1.2 to inspect how these models are trained and inferenced. The operational result is remarkable: input tokens stay cheap, output token costs drop to zero, and downstream latency stabilizes because there is no sampling loop.\n\nUnderstanding the mechanics of decision APIs provides a cleaner, more cost-effective pattern for workflow orchestration than standard generation loops ever could."
