      "image": null,
      "content": "Deploying autonomous coding agents in production usually forces a painful compromise between enterprise security and developer velocity. Handing third-party platforms raw access to internal Git repositories, test runners, and private API credentials is an unacceptable risk for most security teams.\n\nAnthropic has addressed this tension by releasing self-hosted Claude Managed Agents into private beta. Instead of running execution sandboxes exclusively in hosted cloud environments, teams can now run the complete agent control plane on-premises or within their own virtual private cloud. The local deployment includes the orchestrating agent harness, file execution sandboxes, credential management, and session history databases.\n\nThis architecture changes how enterprise agentic workflows operate. Developers interact with the standard Managed Agents API, but workers run shell commands directly against internal services behind your firewall. Model inference requests can still route through external endpoints like Amazon Bedrock or private gateways with zero data retention.\n\nDecoupling the execution harness from the model provider solves the biggest compliance barrier to adopting autonomous agents at scale."
